<title>USA: Continental Air code sharing deal cleared.</title>
<headline>Continental Air code sharing deal cleared.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines Inc said it received approval from the U.S. Department of Transportation to implement a code-share agreement with Britain Group ABH unit Business Air.</p>
<p>The company said the code share is effective September 16 on flights between Newark and Manchester, England, connecting to Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow, Scotland.  </p>
<p>The code sharing deal will allow Continental to book passengers through to flights on the partnering airline.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
